"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ahom%E2%80%93Mughal_conflicts","c":2},{"y":1667,"t":"gain","x":"1667: the Ahoms recapture Guwahati.","m":11,"cp":"mughal-empire","cpn":"Mughal Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ahom%E2%80%93Mughal_conflicts","c":3},{"y":1679,"t":"loss","x":"1679: Laluk Barphukan hands Guwahati to the Mughals.","m":3,"cp":"mughal-empire","cpn":"Mughal Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ahom%E2%80%93Mughal_conflicts","c":3},{"y":1682,"t":"gain","x":"1682: the Mughals are ousted at Itakhuli.","cp":"mughal-empire","cpn":"Mughal Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ahom%E2%80%93Mughal_conflicts","c":3},{"y":1707,"t":"capital_move","x":"1707: the capital is Rangpur.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ahom_kingdom","c":3},{"y":1769,"t":"occupation_start","x":"1769: the Moamoria rebels take Rangpur.","m":11,"cp":"moamoria-rebels","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moamoria_rebellion","c":3},{"y":1770,"t":"occupation_end","x":"1770: the royalists retake Rangpur.","m":4,"cp":"moamoria-rebels","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moamoria_rebellion","c":3},{"y":1788,"t":"occupation_start","x":"1788: the rebels besiege Rangpur and the king flees to Guwahati.","m":1,"cp":"moamoria-rebels","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moamoria_rebellion","c":2},{"y":1794,"t":"capital_move","x":"1794: the capital is Jorhat.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ahom_kingdom","c":3},{"y":1794,"t":"occupation_end","x":"1794: Captain Welsh captures Rangpur.","m":3,"cp":"moamoria-rebels","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moamoria_rebellion","c":3},{"y":1805,"t":"vassal_start","x":"1805: the Matak tract becomes a tributary.","cp":"matak-kingdom","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moamoria_rebellion","c":3},{"y":1822,"t":"occupation_start","x":"1822: the Burmese take Assam.","m":6,"cp":"konbaung-dynasty","cpn":"Konbaung dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burmese_invasions_of_Assam","c":3},{"y":1826,"t":"vassal_end","x":"1826: the Matak tract passes to the British with the rest.","cp":"matak-kingdom","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ahom_kingdom","c":1},{"y":1826,"t":"occupation_end","x":"1826: the Burmese leave Assam.","cp":"konbaung-dynasty","cpn":"Konbaung dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ahom_kingdom","c":3},{"y":1826,"t":"dissolve","x":"1826: Yandabo ends the Ahom kingdom.","cp":"british-empire","cpn":"British Empire in India (East India Company rule)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ahom_kingdom","c":3}],"wars":[{"name":"Ahom-Chutia war","from":1513,"to":1523,"outcome":"Suhungmung annexed the Chutia kingdom in 1523-24.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suhungmung"},{"name":"Ahom-Kachari conflict","from":1526,"to":1536,"outcome":"The Ahoms held Marangi from 1526 and reached the Kolong in 1536; the Kachari king Khunkhara attacked Marangi in 1531.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suhungmung"},{"name":"Turbak's invasions","from":1527,"to":1532,"outcome":"The first Muslim invasion of 1527 was pushed back to the Burai river; Turbak of Gaur advanced in April 1532, was killed near the Bharali and his army pursued 'till the Karatoya'; no land changed hands.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suhungmung"},{"name":"Koch-Ahom conflicts","from":1543,"to":1568,"outcome":"Listed in the infobox as 'Koch-Ahom conflicts: 1543-68'; the pages opened give neither a zone nor an outcome.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ahom_kingdom"},{"name":"Ahom-Mughal wars","from":1615,"to":1682,"outcome":"Barnadi and Kalang fixed by the 1639 treaty; Guwahati changed hands in 1658, 1662, 1667, 1679 and 1682; the Manas became the boundary after Itakhuli.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ahom%E2%80%93Mughal_conflicts"},{"name":"Moamoria rebellion","from":1769,"to":1805,"outcome":"Rebels held Rangpur in 1769-1770 and from 1788 to 1794; the rebellion ended in 1805 with a near-independent Matak tract.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moamoria_rebellion"},{"name":"Burmese invasions of Assam","from":1817,"to":1826,"outcome":"Three Burmese invasions (1817, 1819, 1821-1822); the Burmese took Assam in June 1822 and left under the Treaty of Yandabo in 1826.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burmese_invasions_of_Assam"}],"certainty":[{"from":1228,"to":1638,"level":"soft","note":"No treaty or survey line is on any page for the early kingdom; the Naga and Patkai frontiers are approximate."},{"from":1639,"to":1768,"level":"sharp","note":"The Mughal frontier is fixed by name: the Barnadi and Kalang (treaty of 1639) and the Manas (after Itakhuli, 1682); the hill frontiers stay soft."},{"from":1769,"to":1826,"level":"soft","note":"The Moamoria, Matak and Burmese episodes leave the extent uncertain."}],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ahom_kingdom","title":"Ahom kingdom"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suhungmung","title":"Suhungmung"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ahom%E2%80%93Mughal_conflicts","title":"Ahom-Mughal conflicts"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moamoria_rebellion","title":"Moamoria rebellion"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burmese_invasions_of_Assam","title":"Burmese invasions of Assam"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jayadhwaj_Singha","title":"Jayadhwaj Singha"}]}